eeds a past participle in the past perfect.","D":"Had to changes the meaning to obligation rather than reporting the completed action."}}},{"id":"af7aea26-31fb-5417-aca8-0ec02ca2dc36","topicSlug":"reported-statements","level":"B1","prompt":"Backshift this report: She said, “I repair the rowing boat every week.” → She said she ____ the rowing boat every week.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"repairing"},{"id":"B","text":"to repair"},{"id":"C","text":"repaired"},{"id":"D","text":"repairs"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The reporting verb is past and the instruction requests a **present-to-past backshift**.","explanation":"The instruction requests backshift from present repair to past **repaired**.","keywords":["present-backshift"],"skill":"present-backshift","contextKey":"reported-statements-50","fingerprint":"099c9f4de17d16584eb2e5b156ceda0540dea0a5df2e88e621a6f2e3595d2115","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-statements"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The reporting verb is past and the instruction requests a **present-to-past backshift**.","The instruction requests backshift from present repair to past **repaired**.","Choose **repaired**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"An -ing form alone does not supply a finite reported verb.","B":"A to-infinitive does not complete this that-clause.","C":"The instruction requests backshift from present repair to past **repaired**.","D":"This keeps present tense; the task explicitly requests backshift."}}},{"id":"27f6b97c-b461-566a-a354-17ff2c24817d","topicSlug":"reported-statements","level":"B1","prompt":"Report the plan with backshift: “I will repair the rowing boat.” → She said she ____ the rowing boat.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"would repaired"},{"id":"B","text":"would to repair"},{"id":"C","text":"will repairing"},{"id":"D","text":"would repair"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Backshift the **modal**, not the main verb after it.","explanation":"Backshift **will** to **would**, keeping base repair.","keywords":["future-backshift"],"skill":"future-backshift","contextKey":"reported-statements-50","fingerprint":"0499e928f36f6958d4a7f83d75a1eddf61621ada23c5ea7bf160fdb2ad23c186","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-statements"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Backshift the **modal**, not the main verb after it.","Backshift **will** to **would**, keeping base repair.","Choose **would repair**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The verb after would must remain in its base form.","B":"Would takes a bare infinitive without to.","C":"Will cannot directly take -ing, and it does not perform the requested backshift.","D":"Backshift **will** to **would**, keeping base repair."}}},{"id":"ee351cd4-848d-5ef6-ae13-141d3c5e141b","topicSlug":"reported-statements","level":"B1","prompt":"Choose the verb pattern: “She ____ me that she would repair the rowing boat.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"told"},{"id":"B","text":"said"},{"id":"C","text":"spoke"},{"id":"D","text":"talked"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The listener **me** follows the reporting verb directly.","explanation":"**Told me that** uses tell with a listener object.","keywords":["tell-object"],"skill":"tell-object","contextKey":"reported-statements-50","fingerprint":"6d6a6c323ae415f9b2cbe7ab54bbdf486e87dcafe4393cd043055b9565ee64f2","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-statements"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The listener **me** follows the reporting verb directly.","**Told me that** uses tell with a listener object.","Choose **told**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**Told me that** uses tell with a listener object.","B":"Say does not take me directly in this pattern; it would need to me.","C":"Spoke me that is not the required reporting pattern.","D":"Talked me that is not the standard statement-reporting pattern."}}},{"id":"784ee560-f6a9-5615-a332-7ac2834e5040","topicSlug":"reported-statements","level":"B1","prompt":"Backshift a finished past statement: “We repaired the rowing boat.” → They said they ____ the rowing boat.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"have repaired"},{"id":"B","text":"had repairing"},{"id":"C","text":"had to repair"},{"id":"D","text":"had repaired"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"The original action is already past; the requested backshift is **past perfect**.","explanation":"A requested backshift from past simple uses **had + repaired**.","keywords":["past-backshift"],"skill":"past-backshift","contextKey":"reported-statements-50","fingerprint":"87450e7f9385cd2c6c9ed33a89945f0882eb1fe586d26ed168e91a9b7730e890","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reported-statements"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The original action is already past; the requested backshift is **past perfect**.","A requested backshift from past simple uses **had + repaired**.","Choose **had repaired**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Present perfect is not the requested backshift from past simple.","B":"Had needs a past participle in the past perfect.","C":"Had to changes the meaning to obligation rather than reporting the completed action.","D":"A requested backshift from past simple uses **had + repaired**."}}}],"chapter":{"introduction":["Report someone’s message while adjusting tense, pronouns and time words to the reporting situation.","The form tells you how to build the sentence; the context tells you why that form is useful. Read each section with both questions in mind. The examples make one contrast at a time, while the practice mixes the skills so that you learn to recognise the pattern yourself."],"rules":[{"title":"Reporting is a change of viewpoint","explanation":"Reported speech conveys a message without quoting the exact words. A that-clause commonly follows said or told. Pronouns and time expressions depend on who reports the message, where and when. Do not change them mechanically without checking the situation.","pattern":"“I’m ready.” → She said **she was ready**.","commonMistakes":["If the report is made on the same day, today may remain today. There is no compulsory word-replacement table independent of context."],"examples":["Backshift this report: She said, “I prepare the visitor guide every week.” → She said she **prepared** the visitor guide every week.","Backshift this report: She said, “I restore the old portrait every week.” → She said she **restored** the old portrait every week."],"skill":"form"},{"title":"Backshift after a past reporting verb","explanation":"When a report looks back from a later time, present often shifts to past, past to past perfect, and will to would. This is called backshift. It helps mark the original message as earlier than the reporting moment.","pattern":"“I work here.” → He said he **worked** there.","commonMistakes":["Backshift is not always necessary if the message is still true or relevant. The exercises explicitly request it where needed."],"examples":["Report the plan with backshift: “I will prepare the visitor guide.” → She said she **would prepare** the visitor guide.","Report the plan with backshift: “I will restore the old portrait.” → She said she **would restore** the old portrait."],"skill":"meaning"},{"title":"Say and tell","explanation":"Use **say something** or **say to someone**. Use **tell someone something** with an object naming the listener. These are different verb patterns. Told me that and said to me that can both be correct.","pattern":"She **told me** the news. / She **said** she was tired.","commonMistakes":["She said me is not the standard pattern; use told me or said to me."],"examples":["Choose the verb pattern: “She **told** me that she would prepare the visitor guide.”","Choose the verb pattern: “She **told** me that she would restore the old portrait.”"],"skill":"contrast"},{"title":"Modals and continuing truth","explanation":"Will commonly becomes would and can becomes could in a backshifted report. Would, could, should and might often remain unchanged. A current fact can remain in present tense when the reporter endorses it as still true.","pattern":"He said the Earth **is** round.","commonMistakes":["Reported speech is about accurate meaning, not changing every verb merely because said is past."],"examples":["Backshift a finished past statement: “We prepared the visitor guide.” → They said they **had prepared** the visitor guide.","Backshift a finished past statement: “We restored the old portrait.” → They said they **had restored** the old portrait."],"skill":"application"}],"recap":["“I’m ready.” → She said **she was ready**.","“I work here.” → He said he **worked** there.","She **told me** the news. / She **said** she was tired.","He said the Earth **is** round."]},"stage":"5 · Complex sentences","prerequisites":["relative-clauses"]}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT(version,slug) DO NOTHING;
